        "heading_raw": "Prerequisites",
        "body_raw": "Int 13, Combat Expertise, Improved RepositionAPG."
      },
      {
        "heading_raw": "Benefit",
        "body_raw": "When making a reposition combat maneuver (Pathfinder RPG Advanced Player’s Guide 322), you can move an enemy into a trap or other hazardous area, such as a pit, wall scythe, or blade barrier. When you do so, the moved enemy is treated as though it had activated the trap or triggered the hazard, and it takes a –2 penalty to AC and on saving throws to mitigate the trap or hazard’s effects."
      },
      {
        "heading_raw": "Normal",
        "body_raw": "You cannot reposition a foe into an intrinsically dangerous space such as a pit or blade barrier."
      }
